# THIS FILE IS DOCUMENTATION. Nothing reads it, and no secret belongs in it — it
# is the contract: every variable this project understands, and what it means.
#
# THE FILE THAT IS READ IS `.env.local`, in this same directory. `src/env.ts`
# loads it at start-up, so the 06:00 launchd run — which has no shell and
# therefore no `export` and no profile — gets its credentials the same way an
# interactive run does. It is gitignored (`.gitignore` denies `.env*` and
# re-admits only this file). Keep it mode 0600.
#
# THE REAL ENVIRONMENT WINS. A variable already set in the environment is never
# overwritten by `.env.local`, and the start-up line names any file entry that
# was shadowed, so a stale file value cannot be mistaken for the one in force.
#
# The format is deliberately dumb: `NAME=value`, everything after the first `=`
# taken verbatim. No expansion, no escapes, no comment stripping inside a value
# — a key containing a `#` survives intact. A line that is neither blank, nor a
# comment, nor `NAME=value` stops the process and names its line number: a key
# with a missing `=` must never be silently dropped and then believed set.
#
# Do not copy this file to `.env.local`. That would set every variable to the
# empty string, which is not the same as leaving it unset. Put in `.env.local`
# only the handful you actually mean to set.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAlex (§4.1). MANDATORY for daily running since 13 Feb 2026.
#
# Free key from https://openalex.org/settings/api. Free tier is 100,000
# credits/day; a list query costs 10, so a run's ~10 list queries is a rounding
# error. WITHOUT a key you get 100 credits/day — about ten list queries in
# total, which is enough to smoke-test the adapter and not enough to run daily.
#
# The key is sent as `Authorization: Bearer …`, never as a query parameter, so
# it cannot end up in a log line or an error message. A WRONG key is a hard 401,
# not a silent downgrade to the unkeyed allowance — that is deliberate: a run
# that quietly fell back would look healthy and then die at the allowance.
#
# Once the key is in place, set `sources.openalex.requireApiKey: true` in
# config.json so an unattended run refuses to start unkeyed.
OPENALEX_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Semantic Scholar (§4.2). OPTIONAL — the graph API answers without a key at a
# lower rate. The 1.1 s gap between requests is enforced either way, because the
# documented limit with a key is 1 request/second and going faster unkeyed is
# how you get the whole project rate-limited.
SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic (§7 summarisation, §11-step-8 verification). REQUIRED — without it a
# run can discover and rank papers but cannot write or verify a single word, and
# `research-desk run` stops before publishing rather than shipping a page of
# English abstracts.
#
# This is Research Desk's OWN key. Do not point it at another project's key file
# and do not copy a key between projects: the two have separate spend, and one
# project's cap should not be consumed by the other's bug. Roughly 12 Anthropic
# calls a day at ~$0.11/day — see the cost note in README.md.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
